  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (ignoring probabilities), then evaluating which lottery has a higher chance of exceeding this level. The aspiration level here is -3000, and exceeding it means getting 0 Euros. The reason would favor Lottery B (99.9% chance of 0) over A (99.8%). While the individual ends up favoring a similar aspect (probability of avoiding loss), they do not mention or imply any calculation of an aspiration level, nor do they reference differences between outcomes and a reference point derived from all possible outcomes. The individual’s reasoning is based purely on minimizing the probability of loss, which aligns more with a 'minimax' or 'probability matching' heuristic focused on risk avoidance, not on aspiration level differences. There is no evidence that the individual computed or considered the mean of all outcomes or evaluated outcomes based on their deviation from such a mean. Therefore, although the focus on low loss probability leads in a similar direction, the cognitive process described does not match the aspiration-level-based reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
}

